Squashed from the private llvm-project branch w11-real-headers (base 26eb4285b):
  ac6056d62 [clang] Xilinx HLS bitwidth(N) attribute as _BitInt(N) (-fxlx-bitwidth), opt-in promotion (-fxlx-apint-promote)
  546cda75c [clang] -fxlx-bitwidth: own diagnostics for widths below 1 and above 8191; neutral template test (W11 review)
Apply with: git apply 0001-xlx-bitwidth.patch (in the llvm-project root).

--- ac6056d62 [clang] Xilinx HLS bitwidth(N) attribute as _BitInt(N) (-fxlx-bitwidth), opt-in promotion (-fxlx-apint-promote)

The Vitis HLS 2025.1 synthesis headers build ap_int / ap_fixed on
`int __attribute__((bitwidth(N))) V` (common/technology/autopilot/etc/ap_common.h:529-542);
upstream clang ignores the attribute, so every value became 32 bits.

- Attr.td: XlxBitWidth, a GNU type attribute "bitwidth" with an expression argument
  (ASTNode = 0, like vector_size).
- SemaType.cpp: HandleXlxBitWidthAttr builds _BitInt(N) / unsigned _BitInt(N) with the
  signedness of the builtin integer base type, keeping qualifiers; a template-dependent N
  gives DependentBitIntType (instantiation and deduction are upstream's). Signed width 1
  is accepted under the flag (ap_int<1>). Without -fxlx-bitwidth the attribute is
  diagnosed and ignored exactly as before ("unknown attribute 'bitwidth' ignored").
- SemaExpr.cpp UsualUnaryConversions: with -fxlx-apint-promote a _BitInt no wider than int
  is promoted to int (unsigned int for an unsigned 32-bit one).
- LangOptions.def / Options.td: the two cc1 flags, off by default.

Re-implemented (not copied) from hls-llvm-project (github.com/Xilinx/hls-llvm-project)
ee930469: clang/include/clang/Basic/Attr.td:554-559 (def BitWidth),
clang/lib/Sema/SemaType.cpp:2295 (BuildAPIntType) and :6867 (HandleBitWidthAttr),
clang/lib/Sema/SemaExpr.cpp:704 and clang/lib/AST/ASTContext.cpp:5553-5612
(isPromotableIntegerOrAPIntType, getPromotedIntegerType); those are University of
Illinois/NCSA files with Xilinx additions. hls-llvm-project's APIntType /
DependentSizedAPIntType AST nodes are not ported: BitIntType covers them.

Tests: clang/test/Sema/xlx-bitwidth.c, SemaCXX/xlx-bitwidth-template.cpp,
CodeGen/xlx-bitwidth.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- 546cda75c [clang] -fxlx-bitwidth: own diagnostics for widths below 1 and above 8191; neutral template test (W11 review)

W11 review D4 and D5 (scratchpad w11/review.md):
- D4: under -fxlx-bitwidth every width from 1 up is valid for both signednesses, so
  bitwidth(0) / bitwidth(-3) now report "bit width must be at least 1" instead of the
  _BitInt message ("signed _BitInt must have a bit size of at least 2", or "greater
  than 8388608" for a negative width). Widths above 8191, the ceiling of the
  open-source Xilinx front end (hls-llvm-project ee930469 Type.h:1545 and :3131,
  APIntType::isSizeTooLarge, used at SemaType.cpp:2320), get a warning; whether
  Vitis 2025.1 has the same ceiling is unconfirmed. Custom diagnostic IDs keep the
  private patch out of the diagnostic tables. Re-implemented from that behaviour,
  not copied.
- D5: clang/test/SemaCXX/xlx-bitwidth-template.cpp no longer reproduces the shape of
  the Vitis-installed ssdm_int partial specialisations (etc/ap_common.h:529-542,
  the block the Apache-2.0 HLS_arbitrary_Precision_Types leaves out); it tests the
  same behaviour (dependent width in fields, typedefs, parameters and locals;
  deduction; constant evaluation) with neutral declarations written for the test.
- clang/test/Sema/xlx-bitwidth.c: the new diagnostics.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/clang/include/clang/Basic/Attr.td b/clang/include/clang/Basic/Attr.td
index dd4d45171..d5998057b 100644
--- a/clang/include/clang/Basic/Attr.td
+++ b/clang/include/clang/Basic/Attr.td
@@ -3013,6 +3013,19 @@ def Uuid : InheritableAttr {
   let Documentation = [Undocumented];
 }
 
+// Xilinx HLS arbitrary-precision integer attribute (the Vitis HLS headers'
+// ssdm_int). Re-implemented from hls-llvm-project ee930469 Attr.td:554-559
+// (def BitWidth); here it is represented as BitIntType instead of a new
+// APIntType node, and is only honoured under -fxlx-bitwidth (otherwise it is
+// diagnosed and ignored exactly like an unknown attribute).
+def XlxBitWidth : TypeAttr {
+  let Spellings = [GNU<"bitwidth">];
+  let Args = [ExprArgument<"BitWidth">];
+  let Documentation = [Undocumented];
+  // Represented as BitIntType instead.
+  let ASTNode = 0;
+}
+
